  "did_you_know": "This style of potpourri vase, a pot atop a rockwork base, was popularly produced by major 18th-century porcelain factories including those at Vincennes, Chantilly, and Saint-Cloud.",
  "early_education_description": null,
  "artlens_description": null,
  "description": "The delicate flowers that cover the lid and base of this vase draw inspiration from the <em>schneeballblüten</em>, or guelder rose, pattern produced at the German Meissen porcelain factory. The flowers on the lid are spaced by small, unobtrusive perforations that allow the scent of the potpourri, a mixture of flowers, herbs, and spices placed inside this vase, to disperse.",
